Toriwords dictionary data — licence notice
==========================================

This notice covers the dictionary database built by tools/dictionary/ and distributed as
`dictionary.sqlite` (GitHub Release assets `dictionary-<version>`, bundled in the Toriwords apps) and
`ios/Resources/dictionary-sample.sqlite`. It does not cover the source code of this repository (see LICENSE).

Sources
- English Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org) and Russian Wiktionary (https://ru.wiktionary.org),
  © Wiktionary contributors, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
  International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0). Page histories list the authors.
- Machine-readable extraction by wiktextract (https://github.com/tatuylonen/wiktextract),
  published by kaikki.org (https://kaikki.org). Tatu Ylonen: "Wiktextract: Wiktionary as
  Machine-Readable Structured Data", LREC 2022, pp. 1317–1325.
- Word frequency ranks from wordfreq (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq), data CC BY-SA 4.0.

Changes
The data was modified: filtered (English entries only; obsolete/archaic/rare-only senses, proper names
without a Russian translation, etymology, inflection tables, audio and non-Russian translations removed),
merged (Russian Wiktionary definitions joined to English Wiktionary entries), normalised (Unicode NFC,
quotes and dashes mapped to ASCII, wiki markup and Russian stress marks removed) and ranked. The exact
inputs (URLs, dump dates, SHA-256) are recorded in each database's `meta` table and in
tools/dictionary/build-report.md; the build script is tools/dictionary/.

